					 Chnoubis Amulet 












				 Object Information 
				    1963.04.0008  2.5 cm H X 1.7 cm W X 0.5 cm D  Jewelry ,    Steatite ,    Roman; Egyptian  Egypt ,    Unknown Provenance ,    1-5th century CE   





				 Description 
				  The Chnoubis amulet showcases a lion-headed serpent facing left. Its serpent form, intricately coiled, is adorned with seven or twelve rays encircling its head, sometimes arranged in pairs.The lion-headed snake design embodies the strength of a lion and solar attributes from Egyptian mythology. It represents the amulet&#8217;s protective nature, associated with both the Egyptian god Chnum and the Greek god Agathodaimon. Some amulets, including the Chnoubis amulet, were specifically associated with female reproductive concerns. Alongside its primary association with digestive ailments, it was also believed to protect against sciatica, eye ailments, and fertility issues. 






				 Downloads 
				  The downloadable files are in an .STL format which is optimal for 3D printing. We suggest using a free software such as Meshmixer to edit the file to your needs. Some objects may need supports added or should be hollowed out for the most efficient printing. Any questions about 3D printing should be directed to  kelsey.disko.project@umich.edu . 
